edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1031 "Multiplying Fractions by Whole Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1033 2360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1034 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "576878c2-12a4-51b4-9889-1011d89192c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186454990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186455210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072824 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a0260df7-3f28-567d-be7b-5a8248ccc368" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186455160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186455092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072908 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fb075ecd-d667-5628-a59c-aab6c1c53a3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073415 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10542" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073415 #edb/ref 1071 "Greg stacked $5$ cardboard boxes on top of each other. How tall was his pile if each box is $\\dfrac{3}{4}\\,\\textrm{ft}$ high?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3deda9a1-7edd-5b1e-9f39-5c69644f30ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073415 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out the height of the pile of boxes, we have to multiply $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ by $5.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n5 \\times \\dfrac34 = \\dfrac{5\\times 3}{4} = \\dfrac{15}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\dfrac {15}{4}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n15 \\div 4 = 3\\,\\textrm{R}\\,3 = 3\\,\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nSo, Greg's stack of boxes was $3\\,\\dfrac{3}{4}\\,\\textrm{ft}$ high." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073416 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073416 #edb/ref 1071 "Mr. Stewart spends $\\dfrac56$ hours watching an episode of his favorite TV show. If $5$ episodes are played every week, find the total time he spends watching the show every week. Between what two whole numbers does your answer lie?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073416 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9fb671f7-6d04-5863-9683-3b2c3753df73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073416 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out how long Mr. Stewart watches the show each week, we need to multiply $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ by $5.$ \n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n5\\times\\dfrac56 = \\dfrac{5\\times 5}{6} = \\dfrac{25}6\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\dfrac {25}{6}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n25 \\div 6 = 4\\,\\textrm{R}\\,1 = 4\\,\\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSo, Mr. Stewart spends a total of  $4\\,\\dfrac{1}{6}$ hours watching the show, which lies between $4$ and $5$ hours." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073538 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073538 #edb/ref 1071 "Larry filled his water bottle with $12\\, \\mathrm{oz}$ of drinking water. If he drank $\\dfrac34$ of the bottle's contents after exercising, how much water did Larry drink?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "737b03c4-95f0-5a89-a428-e051b9efee6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073538 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out how much water Larry drank, we need to multiply $12$ by $\\dfrac{3}{4}.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac34 \\times 12 = \\dfrac{3\\times 12}{4} = \\dfrac{36}4\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{36}{4} = 36 \\div 4=9\n$$\n\nSo, Larry drank $9\\,\\textrm{oz}$ of water." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186455466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1039 "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Mixed Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "940366ef-28e8-5827-b52d-a8b500dbb2a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186455461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186455479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining Whole Number Bounds of a Multiplication Problem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b58f3a78-53b1-577f-8907-d53a00186686" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073859 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073859 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073859 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073859 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073859 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186455488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073859 #edb/ref 1039 "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Whole Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073859 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073859 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f8b003cb-5504-549c-8da4-fdc91242c8af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1045 "Multiplying Fractions by Whole Numbers: Word Problems" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186074837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073984 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "6abf4cca-9ce9-543e-b69b-460bc5feb49d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074431 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186072824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074431 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074431 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074431 #edb/ref 1071 "Ted made pizzas for his soccer buddies. He put $\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{lb}$ of cheese on each pizza. If he made $8$ pizzas, how many pounds of cheese did he use in total?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074431 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "742b3068-cb41-500e-9a85-dc782f036323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074431 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out how much cheese Ted used, we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{4}$ by $8.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n8\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{8\\times 1}{4}=\\frac{8}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{4}=8÷4=2\n$$\n\nSo, Ted used $2\\,\\text{lb}$ of cheese to make the pizzas." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074445 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186072908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074445 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60472" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074445 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074445 #edb/ref 1071 "A wooden slat is $3\\,\\text{ft}$ long. Eddie needs to cut a piece that's $\\frac{5}{8}$ the length of the slat. How long is the piece he has to cut?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074445 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7aec9a99-287b-5359-b077-2d2284acc8d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074445 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the length of the piece that Eddie has to cut, we have to multiply $3$ by $\\frac{5}{8}.$  \n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}\\times 3=\\frac{5\\times 3}{8}=\\frac{15}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{15}{8}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n15÷8=1\\,\\text{R}\\,7=1\\,\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nSo, Eddie has to cut a piece $1\\,\\frac{7}{8}\\,\\text{ft}$ long." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074734 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074734 #edb/ref 1061 39848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074734 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f